# Publisher PDFs and anything derived verbatim from them never enter the repo (spec §1.3).
# Anchored to the root: an unanchored "papers/" also matched web/data/papers/, so every
# data bundle the app serves was silently kept out of this public repository.
/papers/
pipeline/cache/
# PyMOL sessions and stills: several megabytes of binaries that `gc figures` regenerates.
# The deploy ships them from the local build; the small .pml scripts are tracked.
web/data/papers/*/figures/*.pse
web/data/papers/*/figures/*.png

# Those two are the only bundle artefacts kept out, and the rule is what the page does with
# them: a .pse and a still are download links, fetched only if a reader asks, and several
# megabytes each. Everything the page LOADS is tracked, including the MD trajectories under
# web/data/papers/*/dynamics/, which are 1 to 2 MB apiece. deploy.sh rsyncs the working tree,
# so an untracked file deploys happily from this machine and then vanishes on a fresh clone,
# which is the failure this repository has already had once with an unanchored papers/ rule.
# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
# macOS / iCloud detritus
.DS_Store
* 2.*
* 3.*
# Session transcripts
*-this-session-*.txt
20[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-*.txt
pipeline/build/
deploy/.env
.env
